  "details": "My system for scaling arms and hands no longer functions correctly in VR (but is fine in desktop mode). Specifically, the hands are not scaling as intended, while the arms still work. This issue occurs with my HandyDrone avatar and other similar avatars. The scaling system operates as follows...\n\nScaling Objects:\n\nThe avatar includes two scaling objects: Arm_Scale and Hand_Scale.\n\nConstraints:\n\nBoth shoulders have scale constraints linked to the Arm_Scale object.\n\nBoth hands have scale constraints linked to the Hand_Scale object.\n\nScaling Method:\n\nParameters and animators control the _Scale objects, allowing adjustments to the arm and hand size without affecting tracking.\n\nIssue:\n\nIn desktop mode and unity emulation, the system works as expected, allowing proper scaling of arms and hands. In VR mode, the hands specifically are no longer scaling, while the arm scale still functions correctly. When scaling the arms in VR, the hands are relatively affected, leading me to believe it may be a VR specific bone chain issue with VRC constraints.\n\nReproduction:\n\nUse the HandyDrone avatar or another avatar with a similar setup (in VR) and try adjusting the hand size (Radial Menu > Utility > Hand Scale)\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_8a24a02a-d0f1-4df7-8f7d-660a8d6ed787",
